	(text "Cell connections (nickel tabs soldered to J1, J2; MID on a thin wire) and the pack leads.\nHigh side: B+ -> fuse F1 -> charge FET Q1 -> discharge FET Q2 -> PACK+. Low side: B- -> R1 (1 mohm) -> PACK-.\nGND on this board is the cells' minus (B-), the gauge's VSS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 18 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "06788e39-8f75-546d-bcc6-3624b02dcde9")
	)
	(text "U1 BQ40Z50-R2 for two cells: VC2 is the top of the stack, VC3 and VC4 are tied to it. PCHG is not used (the charger\nBQ25792 does the pre-charge). PTC is switched off (PTC and PTCEN to VSS). TS1: 10 k thermistor bead on the cells.\nLEDs wired between pairs of the three LED pins as on TI's evaluation module. R21-R23 (two of them in series with\nevery LED) keep the LED current between 4 mA (6 V pack) and 16 mA (8.4 V); the pins alone would sink 22 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200 18 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "b9aa0d8e-5805-5607-8e93-4b8527aee0cf")
	)
	(text "U2 BQ294700: trips at 4.35 V on either cell after 1 to 2 s (C11) and drives Q3 through R7.\nV3 and V4 are tied to V2 for two cells."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 165 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "66f08681-7dd4-531b-8d83-24bf572c05d1")
	)
	(text "SMBus and presence to the blade connector through 100 ohm and an ESD array. The head pulls PRES to ground (1 k).\nSW1 shows the charge state on D2-D5 (LED 1 = lowest)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200 165 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "49d2a261-39ca-5eac-87ea-0973c3b74a4c")
	)
